values ('5c59d111-6ffd-505f-a365-5d60b36dd8af', 'wg3-narrative-writing-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g3-narrative-writing'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Stars Over Our Heads$q$, $q$(1) On Tuesday, my class rode a bus to the city planetarium. (2) We walked into a round room with a giant dome for a ceiling. (3) Our guide, Mr. Adebayo, asked us to lean back in our seats. (4) The lights went dark. (5) Suddenly, thousands of tiny stars sparkled above us. (6) My friend Kenji whispered, "It looks like the real sky at camp!"

(7) Mr. Adebayo pointed a beam of light at a group of stars shaped like a big spoon. (8) He told us it is called the Big Dipper. (9) I learned that sailors long ago used stars to find their way.

(10) ________ the lights came back on, and we blinked in the bright room. (11) On the bus ride home, I drew the Big Dipper in my notebook so I would never forget it.$q$, 'draft')
