   $q$The writer wants to add dialogue after sentence 4 that helps the reader understand what Mr. Haddad is teaching. Which is best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Put in a little air, then dunk it and watch for bubbles,\" Mr. Haddad said.","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Your bike has a flat tire,\" Mr. Haddad said.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-known-fact"},{"text":"\"We will eat lunch at noon today,\" Mr. Haddad said.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-dialogue"},{"text":"\"This is a very nice driveway,\" Mr. Haddad said.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-dialogue"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Put in a little air, then dunk it and watch for bubbles," Mr. Haddad said.$q$, $q$Only "Put in a little air, then dunk it and watch for bubbles" tells the steps for finding the hole that Mr. Haddad shows in sentence 4. The flat tire is already stated in sentence 1, so that line does not teach anything new.$q$, 'draft', '07dad6a6-d352-5cff-b17e-f6f990ba4ff3')
