   $q$Why does the writer include sentence 7, "Then I had an idea"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It brings a new character into the story.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-character-role"},{"text":"It signals a turn in the story, from the problem to how it gets solved.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It tells the reader that the story is now over.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-middle-with-end"},{"text":"It describes what the park looked like that day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It signals a turn in the story, from the problem to how it gets solved.$q$, $q$Before sentence 7, calling does not work; after it, the squeaky ball brings Biscuit back, so the sentence marks the turn toward the solution. The story does not end there, because Biscuit has not come back yet.$q$, 'draft', '9e835f74-d1dd-5f28-97d3-57534700e030')
