        '3-5', $q$My Big Line$q$, $q$(1) Our class put on a play about a town that lost its music. (2) I played the mayor, and I had one very important line. (3) For two weeks, I practiced it in front of the bathroom mirror. (4) On the night of the play, the gym was packed with families.

(5) When it was my turn, I stepped into the bright light. (6) My mind went completely blank. (7) I could hear my own heart thumping. (8) Then I saw my friend Priya behind the curtain, mouthing the first word. (9) "Let the music play again!" I shouted, and the crowd clapped. (10) Our costumes were made from old bedsheets.$q$, 'draft')
